diff --git a/docs/internationalization.md b/docs/internationalization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f23f612
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internationalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Languages
+
+Fizzy offers English (`en`, the unchanged default) and Japanese (`ja`). Open any
+page with `?locale=ja` or `?locale=en` to choose a language. Unsupported values
+are ignored. Anonymous choices live in the Rails session and are copied to the
+identity after authentication. Signed-in choices are stored on the identity,
+so they apply across account memberships and on future sign-ins.
+
+## Rendering
+
+* `CurrentLocale` scopes the request using `I18n.with_locale`. Both HTTP etags and
+  fragment/collection cache keys include the locale. Public HTML is privately
+  cacheable because the session determines its language.
+* Layouts publish the document language and the `javascript` translations. Client
+  messages read this catalog, and dates use the selected locale rather than the
+  browser's default. Changing languages reloads the document and clears old
+  offline pages and navigation labels.
+* Mailers select the recipient identity's locale before running the action, so
+  subjects, HTML, plain text, and dates agree, including in background jobs.
+  Sign-in mail may use an anonymous session's explicit choice without modifying
+  an unauthenticated identity.
+* System comments retain their event reference and render for the reader. Their
+  original English body is preserved for existing English views and exports;
+  older comments can recover their event using the original timestamp. Ordinary
+  user-authored card titles, comments, board names, etc. are never translated.
+* Static errors in `public/` are deliberately bilingual: there is no session
+  when the web server serves them.
+
+## Adding or changing text
+
+Put application messages in matching `config/locales/en.yml` and `ja.yml` keys.
+Use `t` in templates and `I18n.t` elsewhere. Keep interpolations out of catalog
+keys, pass counts for pluralization, and use `l`/`I18n.l` for readable dates.
+Only trusted markup belongs in `_html` messages; Rails escapes ordinary
+interpolation values in HTML translations. Localize whole sentences where
+possible, including accessibility labels and native-app bridge descriptions.
+
+Use `helpers/i18n` for application-owned JavaScript messages. Do not modify the
+strings bundled inside the Lexxy rich-text editor package.
+
+Rails' Japanese date, validation and formatting data live in `rails.ja.yml`;
+Japanese's count rule lives in `plurals.rb`. When adding another language, add
+its complete catalogs, date/number formats and plural rule, then add it to
+`config.i18n.available_locales`.
+
+Run these checks for translation coverage, persistence, cache isolation,
+recipient-scoped mail, and client-side date/message behavior:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/localization test/integration/localization_test.rb test/mailers/localization_test.rb
+bin/rails test test/system/localization_test.rb
+```
